  "officialHtml": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-wq900.html",
  "prefLabel": "Env-Wq 904.02 Counselors, Counselors-In-Training, and Junior Counselors",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-Wq 904.02 Counselors, Counselors-In-Training, and Junior Counselors.\n\n(a) At least 80 percent of all counselors at a residence camp shall be 18 years of age or older.\n\n(b) At least 80 percent of all counselors at a day camp shall:\n\n(1) Be 16 years of age or older; and\n\n(2) Be 2 years or more older than the campers with whom they are working.\n\n(c) Each counselor, counselor-in-training (CIT), and junior counselor (JC) shall attend a comprehensive training program provided by or through the YRC before commencing any activities with campers.\n\n(d) No individual shall be a counselor, CIT, or JC who has any criminal conviction for any offense involving:\n\n(1) Causing or threatening direct physical injury to any individual;\n\n(2) Causing or threatening harm of any nature to any child or children; or\n\n(3) Unlawfully taking property of another, whether through force or threat of force or through deception.\n\nSource. (See Revision Note #1 and Revision Note #2 at chapter heading for Env-Wq 900) #12364, eff 9-1-17",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-wq900.html"
